#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157080 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "5f10a215-83bb-545a-a0e1-ce702f773e6d" :question/math-academy-id "e-7112" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $\\mathcal{B}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ and the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ below, find the value of $x_2,$ the second component of $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}.$\n![](images/c4/c4e78bff8fa8544adb2d150f1cbe0ebc47370949b8198b1c495c0b0a84147798.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ as $\\mathbf{q}_1,\\, \\mathbf{q}_2,\\,\\mathbf{q}_3.$ \n\nSince $\\mathcal{B}$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that ![](images/0e/0eaf45bf0a651744841124a131304a22353ac85f2ebe5ae12ece10d515656469.svg) where $x_i = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{x} \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i}{\\mathbf{q}_i \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i}.$ \n\nComputing $x_2,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot (-4)}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+6+8}{1+1+16} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157081 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157277 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "d7df79a9-2489-5fed-9e00-29890bd01f82" :question/math-academy-id "e-7113" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis ![](images/48/4870d8e5469a2ccc429a0325a19a422820a65a145fa9651b55fe174b17e59841.svg) of $\\mathbb R^2,$ find $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$ if ![](images/45/4555a53bc8e10db083aca9cab2ffde97d414f86c5c90366da1b0ace1f82dad5d.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ as $\\mathbf{q}_1,\\, \\mathbf{q}_2.$ \n\nSince $\\mathcal{B}$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that ![](images/a7/a7be5a62fbf433bf7c0e324aeb284a9c17cf31df39c2e8cc2a9bc1ace486dc98.svg) where $x_i = \\mathbf{x} \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i.$ Computing the components of $\\mathbf{x},$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-2-6=-8 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-4+3=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have ![](images/da/da4ec39d0dbf73a9ec10828d14a2c2f3b0b2907a48e878f97b732d35b02d8200.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157277 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79734ad1-3964-5f5e-9278-275bd9033da0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386002} {:answer/id #uuid "ac89f61f-800f-5761-b7e6-5031550febb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386003} {:answer/id #uuid "2e4613e8-6af0-5396-abab-11c25aa4f010" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386004} {:answer/id #uuid "c4482992-608d-5931-8a49-e73ef737ee25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386005} {:answer/id #uuid "1e2076d2-dca0-5956-b3ba-ca1c44c69dcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4482992-608d-5931-8a49-e73ef737ee25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386005} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4bec8a8-7bc7-5d93-87c4-53f78de8a9e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386001}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c635af5-ba45-5ad9-a96d-e17304471ae7" :question/math-academy-id "q-102320" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157277 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f53a9e3-d347-5d0d-b5ff-95813c38d94f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ 1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236724} {:answer/id #uuid "ac4587b1-cb4b-5eb3-a854-e634958e3ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236911} {:answer/id #uuid "b1b6832e-7ea7-5052-849c-03529284e546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236942} {:answer/id #uuid "bf87509b-e2f2-5d76-9540-054233ae80fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237035} {:answer/id #uuid "f9a054e7-a5cc-5ba5-a3a8-0e8ebde5cd9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}+1 \\\\ 1-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f53a9e3-d347-5d0d-b5ff-95813c38d94f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ 1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236724} :answer-field/id #uuid "a760a8ab-9695-5773-ae90-ab467e5095ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cfeb000c-7c59-5f74-9ec1-f5486996f27d" :question/math-academy-id "q-102322" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]=\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}]=1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ 1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373456 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157277 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2160d32e-fc84-5606-81bf-6a36fb9cb201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373458} {:answer/id #uuid "2f294a17-0886-5984-bebd-cc1203718959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373459} {:answer/id #uuid "e82f3750-80fa-5fdb-baec-6408284b79bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373460} {:answer/id #uuid "9d77672d-4970-5347-a432-379b77724fcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373461} {:answer/id #uuid "8060f3f8-93df-5d1c-af24-9788b325f73a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e82f3750-80fa-5fdb-baec-6408284b79bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373460} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac427e59-1cd1-5f40-bebf-ec7730edebbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd988d09-ca16-589a-bf45-2f1cf35ae96f" :question/math-academy-id "q-102335" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{3}$ is the third component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing ${x}_{3},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} & =x\\cdot {q}_{3} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}+0+0 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dd1edd8-486e-56c4-bd88-bb7947395aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235890} {:answer/id #uuid "5db12ac5-9903-5475-a55d-7b02f66eb236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236406} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ad1688-4ee5-50b3-88c6-fc9a8c5cf946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236960} {:answer/id #uuid "f6488087-a446-537e-9723-32380e643076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237369} {:answer/id #uuid "fdad7f84-a66b-54ba-9e5d-d9442450a98b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6488087-a446-537e-9723-32380e643076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237369} :answer-field/id #uuid "0717b8d9-2e18-5f1a-a3b3-9d17f1c2dafb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237451}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e19c705-cd14-5edd-9733-28f10e7bbc9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-102339" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $6{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-9)\\cdot 4+8\\cdot 2}{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-36+16}{16+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-20}{20} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n6{x}_{1}=6\\cdot (-1)=-6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157768 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0762d58d-9e79-5b37-bd48-01966dae21f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324038} {:answer/id #uuid "147f8ee5-d8ce-58c8-8ec7-1f709eba5719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324157} {:answer/id #uuid "9cb33460-1999-54aa-bf2c-bdff6f4e1d5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325300} {:answer/id #uuid "b8237bb9-f1d6-50eb-bc50-a440d0a6cb5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325551} {:answer/id #uuid "c72c4912-99dc-529c-836f-3e894a49e4e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "147f8ee5-d8ce-58c8-8ec7-1f709eba5719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324157} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2f35c98-6497-5897-b670-16171991f9cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326575}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "58dd07d7-85f8-5406-9b6d-4dde047be9a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-39400" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $29{x}_{1}$, where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-2)}{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15-4-4}{9+16+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n29{x}_{1}=29\\cdot \\frac{7}{29}=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157769 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157277 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5451e40e-c98f-5121-858d-ceb7dac87ed7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324671} {:answer/id #uuid "ce3bce46-3276-5cb7-8bf5-029ebb86c589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325763} {:answer/id #uuid "d2fe69e2-08f4-5b8e-844c-29c932faa38c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325804} {:answer/id #uuid "e2fe6993-5e11-5c46-800b-67cb17619695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325963} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf59942-14f2-5c7b-a997-045fc5f99617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcf59942-14f2-5c7b-a997-045fc5f99617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326198} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc16d48f-b759-5105-a3c1-c4bc75504bbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "824fadc8-cdf9-5224-b7eb-b17e3afd9cf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-39401" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}}-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}=-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}}+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}=-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481422 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a8cbc89-54fa-519f-83a7-e48a95410f62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480792} {:answer/id #uuid "426ae1b3-ab3f-577b-8b6d-7704b4df0833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480866} {:answer/id #uuid "70a5ffa8-a36b-5443-9016-168b83a69d60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480948} {:answer/id #uuid "ad1ad46a-3ef4-5555-bffd-65ab07d26aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481063} {:answer/id #uuid "b7359631-1d40-5953-b4f1-5c9499b96c8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a8cbc89-54fa-519f-83a7-e48a95410f62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480792} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc3a3607-0ff3-5794-9ec9-6e8573576500" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d1f6161d-c4cc-5098-b5d8-59c092ed97d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-39491" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $3{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-8+2}{1+4+1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n3{x}_{2}=3\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3})=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157771 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b7aaa80-e01e-5a58-acbc-d5e2cf0c471a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324075} {:answer/id #uuid "55bb3ad9-903d-5981-9bed-126a70f4d30a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324684} {:answer/id #uuid "75d03881-5557-5b84-aefb-c7343c91d5af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324950} {:answer/id #uuid "b22ee4c0-ca31-5dce-accc-a4c76f8ad416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325496} {:answer/id #uuid "eee83a08-28bc-5604-ba80-722a67b232bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b22ee4c0-ca31-5dce-accc-a4c76f8ad416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325496} :answer-field/id #uuid "91467ccc-fa92-5606-b660-412c7c74373d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c2da7ca-24a0-572d-977f-07408d1bbebe" :question/math-academy-id "q-40291" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $26{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 27\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 2}{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-2}{9+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n26{x}_{1}=26\\cdot \\frac{7}{13}=14.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56ae470a-786d-52a8-ac62-58792ab8b8f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480897} {:answer/id #uuid "bc2be4f7-3223-5c2b-ab19-8ce7df237772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481095} {:answer/id #uuid "d5220df4-8827-5dc8-840c-83a4bee32eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481135} {:answer/id #uuid "e062c38d-7830-506b-89e8-2800051a142b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481160} {:answer/id #uuid "e9f731c8-8b56-5a3c-a03f-ab4777054244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5220df4-8827-5dc8-840c-83a4bee32eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481135} :answer-field/id #uuid "928e03d6-910c-5861-9c3d-cf227edfab96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481290}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8702bab9-12cd-5dfe-a35e-1fe882de5059" :question/math-academy-id "q-81138" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $20{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot (-2)}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3+4}{1+0+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n20{x}_{2}=20\\cdot \\frac{7}{5}=28.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351234 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157277 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63f7514c-f5bf-52e1-bdbb-6a6505cc1e86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349361} {:answer/id #uuid "78a6630e-8b0a-5375-a744-3fd0483c29ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349561} {:answer/id #uuid "8d9542b1-7138-5e04-a78e-9b556e3f6cb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349721} {:answer/id #uuid "e4bd5ee1-00f7-5863-8426-440a8c970769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350451} {:answer/id #uuid "fa89073a-c532-5ab3-a158-561cad7e3407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d9542b1-7138-5e04-a78e-9b556e3f6cb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349721} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9c944e5-277e-5f45-ac43-e02f428a59a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6504cce-f8c4-5ad3-a096-ce35234289bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-81141" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{1}$, where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{35}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{35}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{35}}\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{10} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =x\\cdot {q}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{10} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)=-1.\n$$"}]}
